en.math:
\begin{aligned}
 \langle E\rangle
 &=
 \frac{1}{Z}\sum_i E_i e^{-\beta E_i} \notag\\
 &=
 -\frac{1}{Z}\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\beta}
 =
 -\frac{\partial\log Z}{\partial\beta}.
 \end{aligned}

\begin{aligned}
 (\Delta E)^2
 &=
 \langle E^2\rangle-\langle E\rangle^2 \notag\\
 &=
 \frac{1}{Z}\frac{\partial^2Z}{\partial\beta^2}
 -
 \frac{1}{Z^2}
 \left(\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\beta}\right)^2 \notag\\
 &=
 \frac{\partial^2\log Z}{\partial\beta^2}
 =
 -\frac{\partial\langle E\rangle}{\partial\beta}.
 \end{aligned}

p.src:
In lecture units $T=1/\beta$, so $-\frac{\partial}{\partial\beta}
 =
 T^2\frac{\partial}{\partial T}.$ At fixed volume define the heat capacity of the whole sample by $C_V\equiv
 \left(\frac{\partial\langle E\rangle}{\partial T}\right)_V.$ Equation  becomes $\boxed{(\Delta E)^2=T^2C_V}
 \qquad (k_B=1).$ For laboratory temperature $T_K$, where $\beta=(k_BT_K)^{-1}$, $\boxed{(\Delta E)^2=k_BT_K^2C_V}.$

